/-!
# (key: k-combine) The exit label half over a MUTABLE-SOURCE scalar half: `GLabXZ`, and `GLabXZ.inv : GInvX`

k-combine, 13 Oct 2026.  x-exit-lean's `GLabX` / `GLabX.inv` (XExit/Halves.lean, section Lab), word for word, over
x-mutable's scalar half `GX.GScalZ` (no `hx`: the main phase may write the sources).  Generated by text substitution
(k-combine/tools/make_engine.py):
* `GLabX` -> `GLabXZ`, `finX` -> `finXZ`, `gen2X` -> `gen2XZ` (new names, same namespace `XEX`);
* the end gate to split is x-mutable's `XMut.g8z Mti` (x AND slot rows of the inverse) instead of Sussman's `g8 Mti`,
  backward `(XMut.h8z Mt)ᵀ` instead of `(h8 Mt)ᵀ` (fields `hGsplit`, `hHsplit`);
* the scalar identities are `ScalZ.fwd_scalar` / `ScalZ.bwd_scalar` (x-mutable, XMut/Scal.lean).
The rest gate may touch x roles (`restOk` = not a y role, not an exit slot; x roles stand at the old frame of the
full label at the end, `finXZ`), so nothing else changes.  The conclusion is the SAME package `XEX.GInvX`, so
x-exit-lean's reduction `GInvX.toE'` and everything downstream apply unchanged.
Credits: x-exit-lean (GLabX, on DFT Bridge3's / Nil Mamano's `GLab.inv` and Jacob Sussman's `Lab.inv`); x-mutable
(GScalZ, g8z/h8z, the dirt rule with mutable sources); the hub's exit frames (#593/#599, Kothe's #799 lineage).
No `sorry`.
